module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Geometrically.Irreducible
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Geometrically.Reduced
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Flat
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FinitePresentation
public import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.UniversalHomeomorphism
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Subscheme

import Sheaf.FieldTheory.MakeSeparablyGenerated
import Sheaf.FieldTheory.SeparablyGeneratedTensorReduced

/-! # The radicial extension step for a reduced affine flat family

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0559, second proof, finite purely inseparable extension.
-/

@[expose] public section
universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Topology
namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- After the first flat shrinking, a finite radicial extension of the base makes
its reduced pullback geometrically reduced at the generic point.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0559, second proof, paragraphs beginning
"Write X = Spec(B)" and "Let K'/K"; Algebra, Tag 030R.
Proof: write the affine integral base as Spec A and the reduced affine source as
Spec B. Let K be the fraction field of A. Flatness injects B into B tensor_A K,
which is reduced by localization. Geometric irreducibility makes this nonempty
ring a domain. Its fraction field L is finitely generated over K. Choose a
finite purely inseparable K'/K so that (L tensor_K K')_red is a separably
generated field. In characteristic zero take K'=K. For finitely many generators
b of K'/K choose a prime power q with b^q=a/d in K, with a,d in A and d nonzero.
Replace b by d*b; its q-th power is a*d^(q-1) in A. Let A' be the actual
A-subalgebra of K' generated by these scaled elements. It is a finite integral
domain, its fraction field is K', and every element has a prime power in A.
Consequently Spec A' to Spec A is integral, surjective and universally injective,
hence a universal homeomorphism. Set S'=Spec A' and let q be this morphism.
Its unique point above the generic point of S is generic. The generic fibre of
the canonical reduction of the pullback is Spec of (B tensor_A K')_red:
localization commutes with reduction. The injection B tensor_A K into L remains
injective after tensoring with the field K'. Passing to reductions preserves
injectivity, because an element of a subring is nilpotent if and only if its
image is nilpotent. The resulting reduced generic ring embeds in
(L tensor_K K')_red. A separably generated field is geometrically reduced,
and this property passes to subalgebras by tensoring the injection with every
field extension of K'. This proves the stated geometric reducedness.
No final flat shrinking is asserted, and no arbitrary scheme is selected by a definition.
The empty generic fibre is excluded by geometric irreducibility; empty special
fibres do not enter the field calculation.

(blueprint: lem-sbc-radicial-reduced-flat-generic-fibre) -/
theorem exists_radicial_reduced_flat_generic_fibre
    {Z S : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine Z] [IsReduced Z] [IsAffine S] [IsIntegral S]
    (g : Z ⟶ S) [Flat g] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation g]
    (η : S) (hη : IsGenericPoint η Set.univ)
    (hgeom : GeometricallyIrreducible (g.fiberToSpecResidueField η)) :
    ∃ (S' : Scheme.{u}) (q : S' ⟶ S),
      IsAffine S' ∧ IsIntegral S' ∧ IsUniversalHomeomorphism q ∧
      ∃ η' : S', IsGenericPoint η' Set.univ ∧ q η' = η ∧
        GeometricallyReduced
          (((pullback g q).nilradical.subschemeι ≫ pullback.snd g q).fiberToSpecResidueField
            η') := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
